{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541642652,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNzg1NDc0MTU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2985","origin":"github"},"title":"should may be datalad run record not include empty fields?","message":"ATM run record in commits message would  include\n```\n     \"chain\": [],\n     \"inputs\": [],\n     \"outputs\": [],\n```\nwhich add no information and only make `git log` longer etc.  So I wondered if may be record could contain only non-default/empty/degenerate fields, e.g. instead of\n\n```json\n    {\n     \"chain\": [],\n     \"cmd\": \"git-sedi 'assert_true(\\\\( *.* == .*\\\\) *)$' 'assert \\\\1'\",\n     \"exit\": 0,\n     \"inputs\": [],\n     \"outputs\": [],\n     \"pwd\": \".\"\n    }\n```\nbecome \"more to the point\"\n\n```json\n    {\n     \"cmd\": \"git-sedi 'assert_true(\\\\( *.* == .*\\\\) *)$' 'assert \\\\1'\",\n    }\n```\nwhere expected defaults (running from root of dataset and exit with 0 status) were suppressed.\n\nI think this would help to promote \"datalad run\" for general practice, whenever now a bit length and largely \"not interesting\" record might not look as appealing.  What do you think?","files":null}]}